Can you try speedstep-smi driver?
Is speedstep-smi driver usable or not?
It uses SMI-BIOS call, so if your BIOS has entry, this may work.
This is in-dependent to chipset in theory.

At least, Microsoft's XP document does NOT assumes any specific chipsets.
If your PC is supported in W2K and Intel applet, speedstep-smi driver has a chance.

